WHAT YOU MAY DO WITHOUT ASKING

  - Read the code and the content, and link to any of it.
  - Quote a short passage — a couple of sentences — with attribution to
    Suman Debnath and a link back to https://sumandebnath.com.
  - Learn from it. Techniques, approaches and ideas are not ownable and I make
    no claim on them. It is the specific expression — this code, these words —
    that is mine.
  - Fork this repository on GitHub. That permission comes from GitHub's Terms
    of Service, which let any user fork a public repository, and I am not
    pretending otherwise. It does not extend to taking the fork off GitHub,
    relicensing it, or shipping it.


WHAT REQUIRES WRITTEN PERMISSION FIRST

  - Copying any part of this code into another project, commercial or not.
  - Mirroring, re-uploading or redistributing this repository anywhere outside
    GitHub.
  - Republishing the written content in whole or in substantial part, including
    translated or reworded versions.
  - Using the design or layout as a template for another site.
  - Including any of this in a paid product, client deliverable, or course.
  - Bulk-scraping it to build a dataset, or training a model on it.
  - Presenting any of it as your own work — in a portfolio, a résumé, or a
    take-home assignment.


